[38;5;231m⏺[39m I'd treat this as a bounded change: it filters a table that already exists in [38;5;153mpublic/activity.html[39m, so I'll put a
  short design here in chat instead of writing a spec. Nothing gets built until you approve that design.

  The first question is where the filters go, and that's easier to see than to describe. I've opened a browser tab with
  three sketches:

  [94m]8;id=10btav6;http://localhost:55072/?key=23e54ba2b8c5929f4e416729e116dc3ae3fe706651590a8b59e85878b469a37d\http://localhost:55072/?key=23e54ba2b8c5929f4e416729e116dc3ae3fe706651590a8b59e85878b469a37d[39m]8;;\

  - [1mA. Filter bar above the table:[0m an event type dropdown, a "Failed sign-ins only" checkbox and a result count, always
    visible. This is my pick. Every support ticket so far has been someone looking for a failed sign-in, so that filter
    shouldn't be hidden behind a click.
  - [1mB. Quick-filter chips:[0m one-click presets. I'd have to group the nine event types into a few buckets.
  - [1mC. A "Filter" button with a popover:[0m takes the least space, but it hides the controls.

  Click one in the browser if you like, then reply here. The browser tab uses a lot of tokens, so tell me if you'd
  rather keep this in the terminal.

  There's no [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m in the repo yet, so you may want to create one with [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m in it. That's where the
  sketches are saved.

